<title>Nigeria: the situation</title>
<link>https://map.igred.org/crisis/nigeria/</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">igred-summary-nigeria-2026-10-18T16:02:14.126Z</guid>
<pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:02:14 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;p&gt;Gunmen have intensified attacks on security forces, with ISWAP claiming a strike that killed 21 soldiers and militiamen at an army base, while unknown gunmen assaulted police stations in Plateau, Abia, and Borno, killing multiple officers. Bandits have also used landmines, killing eight soldiers on a Borno highway and another eight near the Cameroon border, and they abducted an air traffic controller in Sokoto, who remains captive after 52 days. President Tinubu approved security equipment to protect trains from bandits, indicating a response to the rising bandit threat. The conflict produced 1,486 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMibkFVX3lxTE00TEhBV0pYNkR1RDJRVTFPSDBEVkZxNDdsQldHb21yTFlvbG92TTh5MWVrYnRvMVFHY2xzNEt2WHpDcUhKYnlwVnpTOGlhSXBjWU1aRERON0tKSjgwR3hXUnJKQkhVOE1TcEtfZFR3?oc=5&quot;&gt;Daily Trust&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilgFBVV95cUxQVXd6b3V0X1FOVUpNRl9EdFU4a1dBRHV6Zm9CN01ZWEhJSmlERHFEcl91c2psTXRZNlI5Q3NyajU1UzYxemJ6QXdhVEtWX1F4ZGhabmI5d0dyVnhSRGVBNjA1RkpOTzlRbFR2aEUwUnQ0bU5ISDJ1LU56OWlLS0U3YVZMU0ZaWlB5clBTbG01bTg3aV9OTmc?oc=5&quot;&gt;Legit.ng&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuAFBVV95cUxQR0kya0wtRk9FTjhrczN4VG96d0ZldExKcTRLLXhyd1NXYlNfc0R1c2cxc293LXN1YUh3MGtYUGdETnpBS2MtT0RzVm1yLW1TRHpOUTNrbHBKWTNRVFl2ZWtMT0xIZWRuNG5YTjdDUmx4T3pVelJFUVJmazJoM2g2dDRITUJ3SHB6TDA5Mms5b0k2dW1Oci1JUklFNlZ3S2t4VVRJZEhaOHlUNk9ZMUVWWlhNQnQ2VkE0?oc=5&quot;&gt;GhanaWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxPTjVtNTdVbXlnZEVEZEtEN2FBTWZoOHlGaG1KUzZ2RTRNVjRjalFIY3hHa3hZZWNXNzdEVDlMNTZ4NHBnbG1EZ1ZqNm5DTGViUXIwZW1UWkNJTldDOGpWdjlSMFJNMEdNdTF0d0V4UDhGTVg1TlIxdjZDZUQ5YzFfYS0wd3d0NVR3aHVlWE1mX0VYUnhEU3plMVBIYVFkNktWRm5jM0E4Vi15NjAwZkZxRElkeV